Z||000000||Jake2m4||04-30-2001||01:06 PM||||Hey I've tried a few methods to remove oxidation of the paint.  (white powder look on paint)  I'm not going for a paint job yet, just a quick fix.<P>I've tried turtle wax rubbing compound, and some other things of that type.  My best luck has been with water and an abrasive surface.  But it takes forever, not too worried about the paint since I can barely see the red anyway. <P>------------------<BR>'85 Fiero Sport Coupe<BR>'95 Pontiac Grand AM SE||||reg||1
Z||000001||Taijiguy||04-30-2001||01:28 PM||||There's a wax called "the Wax Shop"It's a liquid, super easy to apply, andjust as easy to wipe off.<BR>I've used it with good success on minor to moderate oxidization. If it won't handle it alone, they also sell another product called "Dark Magic" which is a deep cleaner. You can apply the Dark Magic, let it dry, and then apply the wax right over it, and remove them both at the same time, which saves a step.<BR>~Taiji||||reg||1
Z||000002||btoth||04-30-2001||04:35 PM||||OK, this may be a dumb question... but how can I tell if my paint is just oxidized or just "burnt" off??  <P>My decklid is almost white (kind of a spottiness to it and rough to the touch) right over the engine and so is the area of the roof right above where the heat would come up along the back window.||||reg||5
Z||000003||rogergarrison||04-30-2001||06:26 PM||||if its not flaking off rubbing compound and polish would help for temporary fix. If you wax over it, the wax will just make it get white again faster. For a very temp fix like for a car show, 'Old English' furniture polish will help hide it most of the time ...... really.......the oil content will make it stay shiny for a day or so.dont buff it, just wipe it on and leave it.||||reg||1
Z||000004||3FastbackGTs||04-30-2001||09:07 PM||||  Dude..just paint your car..lol||||reg||1
Z||000005||84Bill||04-30-2001||09:16 PM||||"Liquid Glass" best damn wax I have ever used ...EVER.. It will knock down all but the worst oxidation the only problem is when you go to paint the car you will need to skuff the car down real good and expect to use alot of sand paper. This stuff will actually fill minor scratches.||||reg||1
